assistant: Subject: convert cent prices from vendor API 2026-10-01

Starting with `vendor-api-version: 2026-10-01`, the vendor returns `price` in cents, not dollars. The same Aero 14 laptop is 1199 in the v1 fixture and 119900 in the recorded call. The vendor spec doesn't say what unit `price` is in; I inferred cents from those two matching responses. `search_products` passed `price` through unchanged, so it reported every laptop at 100 times its real price. The handler now reads the version header and divides prices by 100 when the version is 2026-10-01 or later. Older versions are untouched, so the v1 fixtures give exactly the same output. `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` all pass, but no test runs a 2026-10-01 response yet, so the new path is untested. `get_product` and `get_order` read prices the same way and likely have the same problem; I didn't change them.

